---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { renderDoc } from "../lib/docs";
const doc = renderDoc("ETHICS_AND_ABUSE.md");
---
<Base title="Ethics and abuse policy" description="LureRadar's defensive scope: what we do, what we refuse, how we avoid false accusations and how anyone can dispute a listing." og="about">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:40px">
    <span class="eyebrow">Ethics</span>
    <h1>{doc?.title ?? "Ethics and abuse policy"}</h1>
    {doc ? <article class="prose" set:html={doc.html} /> : (
      <article class="prose">
        <p>LureRadar is defensive only. It analyses public data passively, never executes or detonates anything, and publishes only its own derived indicators.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>We refuse anything that helps create lures, evade detection or attack anyone.</li>
          <li>Every indicator shown is defanged; we say “detected” or “likely”, and “scam” only for CONFIRMED evidence.</li>
          <li>Every listing can be disputed; confirmed false positives are removed on the next run.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    )}
  </div>
</Base>
